        add("wiki.cyberneticenhancements.world_encounter.shipping_container.overview.1", "Freight containers that went over the side of a ship and ended up in the shallows. They lie on beaches, on the sea floor and among coral reefs, some whole, some snapped in half or torn open, some toppled onto their side, and all stacked with wooden crates of cargo.");
        add("wiki.cyberneticenhancements.world_encounter.shipping_container.overview.2", "Nobody guards them. A container is a place to search: every one carries a single kind of cargo, and some hide sealed cargo that belongs to one of your contacts.");
        add("wiki.cyberneticenhancements.world_encounter.shipping_container.where.1", "Swim along the coast or dive in the open ocean. Containers settle on flat sand, gravel or the sea floor, and are rare enough that you may have to cover a lot of shoreline.");
        add("wiki.cyberneticenhancements.world_encounter.shipping_container.where.2", "Locate them with the locate command and the shipping container structure, or ask a contact about a lost shipment, which sends you to the nearest one.");
