        add("wiki.cyberneticenhancements.world_encounter.shipping_container.cargo.electronics.value", "Redstone parts, repeaters, comparators, observers, pistons and lamps, plus copper wiring, conductive paste, sensor lenses, micro batteries, circuit plates and servo screws, with the occasional ender pearl");
        add("wiki.cyberneticenhancements.world_encounter.shipping_container.cargo.weapons", "Weapons");
        add("wiki.cyberneticenhancements.world_encounter.shipping_container.cargo.weapons.value", "An arms cache: arrows, bows and crossbows, iron swords and axes, shields, gunpowder, TNT, fire and wind charges, fireworks and armour, with the rare diamond blade or plate");
        add("wiki.cyberneticenhancements.world_encounter.shipping_container.cargo.medical", "Medical");
        add("wiki.cyberneticenhancements.world_encounter.shipping_container.cargo.medical.value", "Field medicine: healing and regeneration potions, glistering melon, golden apples, honey, bandage cloth and bottles, and very rarely a totem of undying");
        add("wiki.cyberneticenhancements.world_encounter.shipping_container.cargo.components", "Components");
        add("wiki.cyberneticenhancements.world_encounter.shipping_container.cargo.components.value", "Unassembled cyberware parts: common to epic item components, chromium alloy and scrap, joints, servo screws, lenses, batteries, circuit plates and wiring. The best grades are rare.");
        add("wiki.cyberneticenhancements.world_encounter.shipping_container.cargo.barrels.note", "Crates stand in groups with gaps between, up to three high. Each holds one to four kinds of its container's cargo, and the number of slots fits what is inside. Items can be taken out but not put in, and a crate breaks at once.");
        add("wiki.cyberneticenhancements.world_encounter.shipping_container.growth.heading", "Growth");
        add("wiki.cyberneticenhancements.world_encounter.shipping_container.growth.none", "Empty");
        add("wiki.cyberneticenhancements.world_encounter.shipping_container.growth.none.value", "Nothing has taken hold");
        add("wiki.cyberneticenhancements.world_encounter.shipping_container.growth.seagrass", "Seagrass");
        add("wiki.cyberneticenhancements.world_encounter.shipping_container.growth.seagrass.value", "Only in flooded containers; a dry one gets moss instead");
        add("wiki.cyberneticenhancements.world_encounter.shipping_container.growth.moss", "Moss");
        add("wiki.cyberneticenhancements.world_encounter.shipping_container.growth.moss.value", "Moss blocks and carpet on the floor and over the cargo");
        add("wiki.cyberneticenhancements.world_encounter.shipping_container.growth.overgrown", "Overgrown");
        add("wiki.cyberneticenhancements.world_encounter.shipping_container.growth.overgrown.value", "Thick moss with azaleas and hanging roots");
        add("wiki.cyberneticenhancements.world_encounter.shipping_container.growth.glow_lichen", "Glow lichen");
        add("wiki.cyberneticenhancements.world_encounter.shipping_container.growth.glow_lichen.value", "Glowing lichen that lights the inside");
        add("wiki.cyberneticenhancements.world_encounter.shipping_container.growth.note", "Each growth is equally likely.");
        add("wiki.cyberneticenhancements.world_encounter.shipping_container.cargo.1", "About a third of all containers hide sealed cargo in one of their crates. That crate has a golden \"!\" floating over it and nothing above it, so it can be spotted from across the container. Taking the cargo counts as finding it.");
        add("wiki.cyberneticenhancements.world_encounter.shipping_container.quest.1", "Found cargo: when you pick up sealed cargo it is matched to one of your permanent contacts, and a Salvage contract opens at once. Bring the cargo to that contact in person to be paid and earn their trust.");
        add("wiki.cyberneticenhancements.world_encounter.shipping_container.quest.2", "Lost shipment: a contact can instead ask you to retrieve cargo that went down with a container. They point you to the nearest one, and the cargo waits in a crate marked with a golden \"!\" inside it. Bring it back in person.");
        add("wiki.cyberneticenhancements.world_encounter.shipping_container.quest.3", "Either way, everything else in the container is yours to keep. If the cargo goes missing again, nobody blames you: there is no penalty, the contract simply ends.");
        add("wiki.cyberneticenhancements.world_encounter.shipping_container.note.1", "The view above shows the ten container layouts; use the arrows to page through them. Damage, water, growth and cargo are applied when a container generates.");
        add("wiki.cyberneticenhancements.world_encounter.shipping_container.note.2", "Flooded containers sit underwater, so bring a way to breathe before you dive in.");
        add("wiki.cyberneticenhancements.view.page", "Container %s of %s");
        add("wiki.cyberneticenhancements.section.container_condition", "Condition");
        add("wiki.cyberneticenhancements.section.container_cargo", "Cargo");
        add("wiki.cyberneticenhancements.section.container_growth", "Growth");
        add("wiki.cyberneticenhancements.section.container_salvage", "The Cargo");
        add("wiki.cyberneticenhancements.world_encounter.med_tec_av.title", "Med Tec AV");
        add("wiki.cyberneticenhancements.world_encounter.med_tec_av.subtitle", "A MedTec field site with a missing patient");
        add("wiki.cyberneticenhancements.world_encounter.med_tec_av.overview.1", "A MedTec recovery vehicle parked out in the wild, with a small crew standing guard around it. The site is company property and the crew behaves accordingly.");
        add("wiki.cyberneticenhancements.world_encounter.med_tec_av.overview.2", "World encounters are places you stumble on while exploring, unlike street encounters, which find you.");
        add("wiki.cyberneticenhancements.world_encounter.med_tec_av.where.1", "The site generates in forests, taiga, savanna, badlands, desert, plains and meadows. It is rare, so expect to travel to find one.");
        add("wiki.cyberneticenhancements.world_encounter.med_tec_av.where.2", "The ground is cleared and levelled around the vehicle, so trees and hills do not hide it. It does not generate in oceans, mountains or swamps.");
        add("wiki.cyberneticenhancements.world_encounter.med_tec_av.people.1", "Three MedTec staff stand guard. The leader waits inside by the door, and two bystanders with grey names, who will not talk, stand outside on either side of the entrance stairs. They never wander off, but they turn to watch you. A fourth sits on the bench inside the vehicle, next to its loot. Opening the chest or breaking into a relic cache there turns all of them against you.");
        add("wiki.cyberneticenhancements.world_encounter.med_tec_av.people.2", "The leader sells nothing and offers no services. They explain the situation and hand out the one quest, which opens as soon as you speak to them.");
        add("wiki.cyberneticenhancements.world_encounter.med_tec_av.barrier.1", "A holographic panel hangs in the doorway of the vehicle to mark it as restricted. It is only light: you can walk straight through it, so it is a warning and not a lock.");
        add("wiki.cyberneticenhancements.world_encounter.med_tec_av.barrier.2", "Yellow with a ! means the site is open to you. You have done nothing to the crew or their cache, and the leader still deals with you. Treat it as a reminder that everything inside belongs to MedTec.");
        add("wiki.cyberneticenhancements.world_encounter.med_tec_av.barrier.3", "Red with an X means you have wronged the site: you opened its chest or relic cache, broke part of the build, or struck one of the crew. The leader refuses to offer you the quest again, for good, and the barrier shows this to you alone. If you walk through the barrier anyway, the crew attacks on sight. Other players still see their own colour.");
        add("wiki.cyberneticenhancements.world_encounter.med_tec_av.barrier.4", "Red with a countdown means you failed the Missing Patient quest. The leader will not deal with you for fifteen minutes, and the barrier counts down the time left. When it runs out, the barrier fades back to yellow with a soft chime and the leader will offer the quest again. Walking through it in the meantime still makes the crew attack.");
        add("wiki.cyberneticenhancements.world_encounter.med_tec_av.quest.1", "Missing Patient: a MedTec patient has gone missing and the tracking system is down. The coordinates are only roughly right, so you must search the marked area on your compass.");
        add("wiki.cyberneticenhancements.world_encounter.med_tec_av.quest.2", "The patient lies somewhere inside the area, never at its centre, and only appears once you are within about 110 blocks. They glow when you get close. Walk right up to them to find them.");
        add("wiki.cyberneticenhancements.world_encounter.med_tec_av.quest.3", "Nothing needs to be carried back. Return to the leader and tell them in person to be paid.");
        add("wiki.cyberneticenhancements.world_encounter.med_tec_av.note.1", "Hurting any MedTec at the site turns the whole crew hostile at once, and breaking blocks of the build is held against you too. Either way the leader never offers you the quest again. MaxTec does not answer for them, so there is no patrol to save you either.");
        add("wiki.cyberneticenhancements.world_encounter.med_tec_av.note.2", "If the leader dies, the quest can no longer be handed in.");
        add("wiki.cyberneticenhancements.section.how_it_works", "How It Works");
        add("wiki.cyberneticenhancements.section.your_options", "Your Options");
        add("wiki.cyberneticenhancements.section.good_to_know", "Good To Know");
        add("wiki.cyberneticenhancements.encounter.stock_entry", "%sx %s");
        add("wiki.cyberneticenhancements.encounter.service_price", "Price: %s €$.");
        add("wiki.cyberneticenhancements.encounter.street_ripperdoc.title", "Mobile Ripperdoc");
        add("wiki.cyberneticenhancements.encounter.street_ripperdoc.subtitle", "A wandering clinic that comes to you and does not stay");
        add("wiki.cyberneticenhancements.encounter.street_ripperdoc.overview.1", "Now and then a street ripperdoc picks you out and heads your way. They sell real chrome from a street stock of tiers one to three, plus clinic supplies, and offer two services you will not find at a permanent contact.");
        add("wiki.cyberneticenhancements.encounter.street_ripperdoc.overview.2", "Encounters happen in the overworld, under open sky, roughly every twenty to forty minutes. Operators can trigger one with /cyberneticenhancements encounter trigger ripperdoc, and the gamerule cyberneticStreetEncounters turns them off.");
        add("wiki.cyberneticenhancements.encounter.street_ripperdoc.how.1", "The doctor appears as a green hologram some fifteen to twenty-five blocks away and walks straight to you.");
        add("wiki.cyberneticenhancements.encounter.street_ripperdoc.how.2", "If they cannot reach you within five minutes, or you simply never talk to them, they leave as a hologram.");
        add("wiki.cyberneticenhancements.encounter.street_ripperdoc.how.3", "Once you have spoken, they wait at most two more minutes and never leave mid-conversation.");
        add("wiki.cyberneticenhancements.encounter.street_ripperdoc.how.4", "Implants still have to be installed at a Ripper Station. The doctor only sells them.");
        add("wiki.cyberneticenhancements.encounter.street_ripperdoc.note.1", "A mobile ripperdoc is never a contact: there is no trust, no discount, no renaming and no entry in your contacts archive. Prices are fixed and nothing is locked behind trust.");
        add("wiki.cyberneticenhancements.encounter.street_ripperdoc.note.2", "Killing one is allowed and does not bring MaxTec down on you.");
        add("wiki.cyberneticenhancements.encounter.shakedown.title", "Gang Shakedown");
        add("wiki.cyberneticenhancements.encounter.shakedown.subtitle", "A street gang demands a toll");
        add("wiki.cyberneticenhancements.encounter.shakedown.overview.1", "A street gang closes in on you and demands a toll. Who comes, what they ask and how they treat you depends on your Street Cred. They talk first and only fight once you turn them down or the time runs out.");
        add("wiki.cyberneticenhancements.encounter.shakedown.overview.2", "Shakedowns follow the same timing as other street encounters, but never happen on Peaceful difficulty or to players with less than 50 eurodollars. Operators can trigger one with /cyberneticenhancements encounter trigger shakedown.");
        add("wiki.cyberneticenhancements.encounter.shakedown.how.1", "The gang appears as holograms ten to sixteen blocks away and walks up to you.");
        add("wiki.cyberneticenhancements.encounter.shakedown.how.2", "The toll is a share of your eurodollar balance, kept within a range that depends on your Street Cred.");
        add("wiki.cyberneticenhancements.encounter.shakedown.how.3", "You have a limited time to answer, longer the bigger your name. Say nothing and the gang attacks.");
        add("wiki.cyberneticenhancements.encounter.shakedown.options.1", "Pay: the gang takes the toll and leaves as holograms. If you cannot afford it, they take offence and attack.");
        add("wiki.cyberneticenhancements.encounter.shakedown.options.2", "Refuse: a bluff. Each implant you have installed adds a chance that the gang backs down, and a name adds more. If it fails, they attack.");
        add("wiki.cyberneticenhancements.encounter.shakedown.options.3", "Fight: striking any of them also ends the negotiation and turns the whole gang on you.");
        add("wiki.cyberneticenhancements.encounter.shakedown.note.1", "Once hostile, the gang hunts only you, and gives up if you get far away or they have been around for eight minutes.");
        add("wiki.cyberneticenhancements.encounter.shakedown.note.2", "Defeating them does not bring MaxTec.");
