        add("wiki.cyberneticenhancements.lore.reserved", "Lore coverage is intentionally light right now. This archive section is reserved for future quest, NPC, clinic and manufacturer writing.");
        add("wiki.cyberneticenhancements.lore.current_state.branch_ready", "The archive already has a dedicated lore branch so future narrative content can be added without redesigning the interface.");
        add("wiki.cyberneticenhancements.lore.current_state.gameplay_authority", "For now, gameplay and mechanical entries are the authoritative part of the wiki.");
        add("wiki.cyberneticenhancements.quests.reserved", "Contract boards and the quest log are live for Techie, Netrunner and Merc contacts.");
        add("wiki.cyberneticenhancements.quests.current_state.placeholder", "Seven contract types are implemented: Delivery, Extraction, Investigation, Breach, Elimination, Recovery and Cyberpsycho Sighting. The available mix depends on the issuing contact.");
        add("wiki.cyberneticenhancements.quests.current_state.progression", "Completed jobs pay eurodollars, trust and 15-120 XP points based on type and tier, may include supplies, and can award missing fabrication schematics or parts. Recovery payments include compensation for the requested materials. Bundled ordinary contracts discover designs up to tier four; tier-three Cyberpsycho Sightings can reach tier-five designs and restricted cores. XP is paid once at turn-in, including by call or the Quests tab; failed, abandoned and cancelled jobs give none. Server datapacks control money, trust and discovery chances.");
        add("wiki.cyberneticenhancements.quests.cyberpsycho", "Cyberpsycho Sightings are high-risk jobs from Techies, Netrunners and Mercs. The compass shows a 48-block search area. Find the named opponent, whose red name warns that they are aggressive. Expect heavy armor, high health and one of five working cyberware loadouts: mantis blades, thermal blades, shock blades, projectile launcher or gorilla arms. Blade lunges and launcher shots have windups; missiles do not damage terrain. Kill the subject, loot their named information shard and hand it to the issuer in person. The dossier is required for payment and identifies the subject and their cyberware. These jobs have the highest standard money payouts and enhanced trust rewards. There is a 25% chance of recovering a damaged implant matching the enemy's loadout. Your encounter persists across reloads, and lost dossiers trigger an angry call after 10 seconds missing; confirm external storage to keep the quest, or it fails.");
        add("wiki.cyberneticenhancements.quests.planned_surface.contracts", "You can hold one active contract per issuing contact, with no total limit. Extraction shards, recovery supplies and cyberpsycho dossiers must be handed to the issuer in person. Other ready objectives can be reported through the Quests tab, a call or the issuer. Remote item rewards go to your Dropoff Point within one Minecraft day; in-person handovers give items immediately.");
        add("wiki.cyberneticenhancements.quests.planned_surface.archive", "The Quests tab separates Active, Completed, Abandoned, Failed and Cancelled contracts, and tracks objectives, destinations and ready turn-ins. Delivery deposits a package in an Iron Quest Crate; Extraction retrieves a shard from the same metal container; Investigation triangulates a hidden source from three separated, stationary scans and then breaches its secured cache; Breach completes a secured cache in one committed attempt; failure costs trust and successes disappear after payout; Elimination defeats targets; Recovery supplies requested items; Cyberpsycho Sighting locates and defeats a named, heavily augmented opponent, then returns their information shard in person. Confirmed issuer deaths, unavailable dimensions and invalid destinations cancel contracts without trust loss or rewards. Missing containers and unstarted caches are restored only where safe. A blocked site or missing encounter cancels after 30 seconds of nearby checks; unloaded sites and time spent away do not count. Cancelled history explains the reason. Started breaches still have one attempt and their normal failure penalty.");
